<div id="S4.I2.i1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Then, <span id="S4.I2.i1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:90%;">GRASP</span> queues up SCP 1’s children.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">b.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SCP 2</span>: This SCP focuses on memory management, which is automatically handled by Python. Given its low relevance score of <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, no changes are made.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">c.</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SCP 4</span>: This SCP is relevant (score <math id="S4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>) and ensures files are not unintentionally overwritten. The code is updated to check if files already exist in the extraction directory before proceeding.</p>
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_diff ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
